## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical knowledge of AWS streaming data pipelines, including real-time validation, PII masking, data quality scoring, and observability across a distributed system.

## Key Concepts

- Kinesis Data Streams for real-time data ingestion
- JSON schema validation with schema registry
- In-flight PII masking (email, phone, credit card regex patterns)
- Parquet format with date partitioning for analytics optimization
- Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) for non-compliant record handling
- AWS X-Ray distributed tracing across Lambda, Kinesis, and S3
- LocalStack for local development and testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII masking functions
function maskEmail(email) {
  const [local, domain] = email.split('@');
  return local.replace(/./g, '*') + '@' + domain;
}

function maskPhone(phone) {
  return phone.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
}

function maskCreditCard(cc) {
  return cc.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
}
```

